# To my brother in Russian: моему́ бра́ту
subtitle: "Say to my brother, with my mum and at my brother's in Russian: my and your go into the case with their noun, моему́ бра́ту, с мое́й ма́мой, у моего́ бра́та, while his and her, его́ and её, never change."
teaches: ["grammar/case-agreement","grammar/possessives"]
thumb: "band \"To my brother: my changes too\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"A sixth Russian story: Ivan's birthday","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/60-russian-review-6.cast"}

## To my brother in Russian: моему́ бра́ту
level: basic

